# Secrets defined here are available for reference under registry/password, env/secret, builder/secrets,
# and accessories/*/env/secret in config/deploy.yml. All secrets should be pulled from either
# password manager, ENV, or a file. DO NOT ENTER RAW CREDENTIALS HERE! This file needs to be safe for git.

# Docker Hub access token, not the account password. Kept out of .env.production
# because it is a deploy credential, not something the app reads at runtime.
KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$(grep -m1 "^KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=" .env.production | cut -d= -f2-)

# Cloudflare origin certificate for *.dominiksek.pl. Kamal reads the PEM bodies
# here and uploads them to the proxy; the files themselves are gitignored and
# exist only on this machine, so keep a copy in the password manager.
CLOUDFLARE_ORIGIN_CERT=$(cat .kamal/cloudflare-origin.pem)
CLOUDFLARE_ORIGIN_KEY=$(cat .kamal/cloudflare-origin.key)

# Read from the gitignored .env.production. That file, not .env, is the production
# set: .env is development, where dotenv-rails loads it for you. Every name below
# also has to appear under env/secret in config/deploy.yml to reach the container.

